After an early preliminary hearing determined there was enough evidence for her to stand trial Court proceedings had to be postponed several times due to blizzards and flood warnings On his way into court, Paula's defense lawyer joked to local police that she had been found Paula's defense lawyer joked to local newspaper The Morning Call We've encountered blizzards and floods and I hope that pestilence and locusts aren't far behind Court Room No. 4 was packed with journalists as well as members of the general public who were intrigued by the unusual case If found guilty, Paula Norrocke faced a maximum of five years jail time and a $10,000 fine for each count She listened attentively to testimony from those who examined the DNA evidence on the letters and envelopes
在初审确定有足够证据让她接受审判后，由于暴风雪和洪水预警，法庭审理程序不得不推迟了好几次。在前往法院的路上，保拉的辩护律师开玩笑地对当地警察说她已经被找到了。保拉的辩护律师对当地报纸《晨报》开玩笑说：“我们遇到了暴风雪和洪水，我希望瘟疫和蝗虫不会太远。”4号法庭挤满了记者以及对这起不寻常案件感兴趣的公众。如果被判有罪，保拉·诺罗基每项指控将面临最高五年的监禁和1万美元的罚款。她专心聆听了检查信件和信封上DNA证据的人员的证词。

24
00:19:17.000 --> 00:20:14.000
Another DNA sample was extracted from adhesive used to seal an envelope The sample wasn't strong enough to obtain a full profile as had been done with the postage stamps However, it was complete enough to rule out Paula Norrocke as the source Joanne Chambers could not be excluded Speaking calmly and concisely, Paula Norrocke testified that she believed Joanne was harassing herself in an attempt to frame her and to gain attention Paula had an explanation for retrieving the coffee cup from Joanne's desk She stated that Joanne had asked her to get it for her It was determined that Paula had been subjected to a different, more rigorous polygraph test than Joanne
从用于封信封的粘合剂中提取了另一个DNA样本。该样本不够强大，无法像邮票那样获得完整的图谱。然而，它足够完整，可以排除保拉·诺罗基作为来源。琼·钱伯斯无法被排除。保拉·诺罗基平静而简练地作证说，她认为琼一直在骚扰自己，企图陷害她并博取关注。保拉对从琼的桌子上拿走咖啡杯做出了解释。她表示是琼让她帮拿的。经确定，保拉接受了与琼不同、更严格的测谎测试。

25
00:20:14.000 --> 00:21:10.000
Furthermore, her comment to Chief Anthony Flugel, you'll never prove it was me, had been taken entirely out of context then used against her The jury heard testimony from former employees who described Paula's exemplary behaviour and teaching ability Analysis of the stationary and typewriter found in Paula's home did not match the letters received by Joanne Joanne's typewriter was never examined A chemist discredited Joanne's allegation that she affixed the stamps back to the envelope with a glue stick as the adhesive would turn a bluish colour under UV light When he examined the stamps, this was not apparent Next, Joanne Chambers took the stand
此外，她对安东尼·弗卢格警长说的“你永远无法证明是我干的”这句话完全被断章取义，然后用来对付她。陪审团听取了前员工的证词，他们描述了保拉的模范行为和教学能力。对在保拉家中发现的文具和打字机的分析与琼收到的信件不符。琼的打字机从未被检查过。一位化学家反驳了琼关于她用胶棒将邮票重新贴在信封上的指控，因为在紫外光下，粘合剂会变成蓝色。当他检查邮票时，这并不明显。接下来，琼·钱伯斯出庭作证。

26
00:21:10.000 --> 00:22:21.000
Her demeanour, her behaviour, and her behaviour were not clear Mina, as she answered questions from the defence, did little to help her cause The morning call reported her testimony as uneven, with replies that ranged from subdued to testy to sarcastic She also rolled her eyes, and courtroom observers noticed that she seemed edgy Mid-trial, the principal of Joanne's former school provoked an audible gasp from the courtroom as he recounted an event from Joanne's earlier career In the early 80s, Joanne had approached him asking to go home early because she had sat in feces Private investigator James Anderson, hired by Paula Norrocke, had found witnesses who'd worked with Joanne Chambers at this point in her career One witness, Jane Padoe, told the court that she and the six other teachers at the school were summoned to the library for a meeting
她的风度、行为和表现都不明确。米娜在回答辩护方的提问时，对她的处境毫无帮助。《晨报》报道她的证词断断续续，回答从低调到易怒再到讽刺不等。她还翻白眼，法庭观察员注意到她似乎有些急躁。庭审进行到一半时，琼前学校的校长复述了琼早期职业生涯中的一件事，引发了法庭上一阵清晰的惊呼。80年代初，琼曾找到他，要求早退，因为她坐在了粪便上。由保拉·诺罗基聘请的私家侦探詹姆斯·安德森找到了在职业生涯这个阶段与琼·钱伯斯共事过的证人。一位证人简·帕多告诉法庭，她和学校的其他六名老师被召集到图书馆开会。

27
00:22:21.000 --> 00:23:23.000
They were told that Joanne had received harassing phone calls and threats that her house would be burned down Jane said of Joanne She carried tales that weren't true to the superintendent, and she tried to get us in trouble Jane added that she wanted to stay as far away from Joanne Chambers as possible Witness Lois Render, a former teacher, described Chambers as someone who told tall tales One involved Joanne studying to be a nun She said she'd broken her leg after jumping out a window to escape the nuns who were trying to force her to stay at the convent Also remembering that Joanne tried to get other teachers into trouble, Lois described her school as a harmonious place until Chambers came along
他们被告知琼收到了骚扰电话和烧毁她房子的威胁。简对琼评价道：“她向校长搬弄不实之词，并试图让我们陷入麻烦。”简补充说，她想离琼·钱伯斯越远越好。证人露丝·伦德是一名退休教师，她形容钱伯斯是个爱编造离奇故事的人。其中一个故事是琼曾学习当修女。她说她从窗户跳下去逃跑时摔断了腿，因为修女们试图强迫她留在修道院里。露丝还记得琼试图让其他老师惹麻烦，她形容她的学校曾经是一个和谐的地方，直到钱伯斯出现。

28
00:23:23.000 --> 00:24:26.000
Private investigator James Anderson listed 16 occasions where Joanne complained to authorities about anonymous threats prior to the incidents with Paula Norrocke Paula's defense lawyer suggested that Joanne had placed the evidence herself to frame Paula because she hadn't catered to Joanne as other teachers had done Additionally, there were no witnesses who observed Joanne being run off the road by Paula Norrocke Joanne's testimony was the only thing implicating Paula in this event On January 22, 1996, the six men and six women of the jury retired to deliberate They returned to the courtroom less than two hours later Paula Norrocke was found not guilty of all charges The jurors hugged Paula after the trial
私家侦探詹姆斯·安德森列出了在与保拉·诺罗基发生事件之前，琼向当局投诉匿名威胁的16次经历。保拉的辩护律师暗示，琼自己放置了证据来陷害保拉，因为保拉没有像其他老师那样迎合琼。此外，没有目击者看到琼被保拉·诺罗基逼出路面。琼的证词是唯一将保拉牵连到这一事件中的东西。1996年1月22日，六名男陪审员和六名女陪审员退席进行闭门商议。不到两小时后，他们返回法庭。保拉·诺罗基被裁定所有指控不成立。审判结束后，陪审员们拥抱了保拉。

