00:24:26.000 --> 00:25:46.000
One told her, Our hearts are with you Joanne Chambers slipped from the courtroom quietly, largely ignored by those in attendance Although she was found to not guilty on all charges, Paula Norrocke was still required to attend a school board hearing to determine whether or not she could keep her job Held over a series of nights in early 1997, the hearing was to address charges of immorality, neglect and other school code violations in relation to the case Unlike the criminal trial that required a unanimous verdict, only six of the appointed eight school directors had to find that Paula Norrocke acted immorally and in their election of duty for her to lose her job Mike Eleven, acting as prosecutor on behalf of the school board, opened by saying This case is a most unusual, most tragic case You will hear about 41 profane, threatening, disgusting letters
其中一人对她说：“我们的心与你同在。”琼·钱伯斯静静地溜出法庭，在场的人大多忽视了她。尽管所有指控均被判无罪，但保拉·诺罗基仍被要求出席学校董事会听证会，以决定她是否能保住工作。听证会于1997年初连续几个晚上举行，旨在处理与此案相关的违反道德、疏忽和其他学校规章制度的指控。与需要一致裁决的刑事审判不同，指定的八名学校董事中，只需六名认为保拉·诺罗基行为不道德且玩忽职守，她就会失去工作。代表学校董事会担任检察官的迈克·埃莱文在开场白中说：“这个案子是一个极不寻常、极悲惨的案子。你们将听到41封充满亵渎、威胁、令人作呕的信件。”

30
00:25:46.000 --> 00:26:59.000
You will hear about blood, you will hear about feces, you will hear about razor blades, you will hear about a Barbie doll, you will hear about nude photographs Everyone involved in the case agrees that the stalking incidents happened and that the person responsible should be fired The point of the disagreements with this case is, who did it? Who is responsible for these acts? The hearing largely repeated the information presented at the criminal trial On April 2, 1997, Paula Norrocke was acquitted of the charges against her and permitted to keep her teaching job When the verdict was read, the packed auditorium, opened to the public, cheered for Paula Jeering could be heard at the mention of Joanne Chambers' name But, with no evidence proving she was the cause of the harassment, Joanne was also allowed to keep teaching
你们会听到血，你们会听到粪便，你们会听到剃须刀片，你们会听到一个芭比娃娃，你们会听到裸照。案中所有人都同意跟踪事件确实发生过，肇事者应该被解雇。本案争议的焦点在于，是谁干的？谁应对这些行为负责？听证会大体上重复了刑事审判中提出的信息。1997年4月2日，保拉·诺罗基被判无罪，并获准保留教职。宣判时，向公众开放的座无虚席的礼堂为保拉欢呼。当提到琼·钱伯斯的名字时，可以听到嘘声。但是，由于没有证据证明她是骚扰的根源，琼也被允许继续教书。

31
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:58.000
In November 2000, Paula Norrocke received a $600,000 settlement from the school district She was also awarded a $25,000 settlement from Joanne Chambers, after seeking compensation for out-of-pocket costs and punitive damages in the course of the trial Paula also sought compensation for defamation from lead detective, Chief Anthony Flugel She alleged he maliciously prosecuted her without probable cause Flugel, who was by this time a lieutenant, refused to settle out of court A federal damage trial commenced in December 2000 Flugel testified that he acted under the direction of the Monroe County District Attorney's Office And there was probable cause at the time to arrest Paula Norrocke
2000年11月，保拉·诺罗基从学区获得了60万美元的和解金。在审判过程中寻求自付费用和惩罚性赔偿的赔偿后，她还获得了一笔来自琼·钱伯斯的25,000美元和解金。保拉还就主侦探安东尼·弗卢格警长对其进行诽谤寻求赔偿。她指控他在没有合理根据的情况下恶意起诉她。当时已升任中尉的弗卢格拒绝庭外和解。联邦损害赔偿审判于2000年12月开始。弗卢格作证说，他是根据门罗县地方检察官办公室的指示行事的，当时有合理根据逮捕保拉·诺罗基。

32
00:27:58.000 --> 00:29:17.000
Paula's defense argued that the arrest and subsequent trial proceeded despite a mountain of growing evidence implicating Joanne Chambers as her own tormentor In a case described by Paula's defense attorney as the strangest he had ever been involved in, Flugel was acquitted of the charge of defamation on December 12, 2000 Both women continued teaching at different schools and had successful careers Paula Norrocke had suffered the fallout of being in the public eye, telling the court at the federal trial that Some people still avoid me But by 2001 Paula was teaching the third grade and it was reported in the morning call that her life had largely returned to normal In 2014, after a celebrated career, Joanne Chambers retired from teaching She obtained the status of a national board certified teacher and had helped hundreds of students learn to read as a specialist teacher for children with dyslexia
保拉的辩护律师辩称，尽管有如山般的证据表明琼·钱伯斯是她自己的折磨者，但逮捕和随后的审判仍在继续。正如保拉的辩护律师所描述的那样，这是他参与过的最奇怪的案件，2000年12月12日，弗卢格被判诽谤罪不成立。两位女性继续在不同的学校教书并取得了成功的职业生涯。保拉·诺罗基承受了身处公众视野的余波，她在联邦审判中告诉法庭：“有些人仍然躲着我。”但到2001年，保拉正在教三年级，据《晨报》报道，她的生活基本恢复了正常。2014年，经过辉煌的职业生涯，琼·钱伯斯从教学生涯中退休。她获得了国家董事会认证教师的身份，并作为儿童诵读困难专科老师帮助数百名学生学会了阅读。

